Changelog: 15-10-2026 21:33:57

images/bazzite-datstation-128.png is the 128 px copy of the new icon (images/bazzite-datstation.png), scaled from the
512 px file; the README, the wiki's apps overview and the portal's tile show it.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 19:18:30

style.py's docstring no longer points at the UMD File Renamer (absorbed into PPSSPP Manager) for the app-wide style
sheet; the code is unchanged.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 16:02:21

Moved into the BC250 Bazzite Suite (apps/bazzite-datstation): the bundled bc250_core, CLAUDE.md, test.sh and
.gitattributes went, and mkdocs.md is the suite's wiki chapter. The tests take bc250_core from the suite's core/. The
project page and the update check point to the suite's repository, where the app's releases are (bazzite-
datstation-v<x.y.z>). The README is short, as the suite's apps have it, and links to the wiki. The tests no longer
reach a Steam on the machine: HOME is a temp folder, so the refusal without Steam holds where Steam is installed, and
core's with_steam_closed sees no Steam running and starts no Steam command (its defaults were bound at import, so
patching steam.steam_running did not reach them: on a machine with Steam running, the main window tests closed and
restarted it, and the refusal test wrote a shortcut into the real shortcuts.vdf).

Changelog: 15-10-2026 10:16:28

CI: the shell job installs Qt's runtime libraries before it runs install.sh, which imports PyQt6 from the venv it
made (libEGL.so.1 was missing on the runner). CLAUDE.md with the state of the work and the rules, and mkdocs.md,
the wiki chapter for the suite (install, using it, files, privacy, troubleshooting, development with the security
around the build).

Changelog: 15-10-2026 05:08:44

Bazzite DatStation 0.1.0, the first version: the Quiz, the PlayStation History, the System Version History, the
Region Codes Explained, the PlayStation User Guides and PS News of the DatStation Android app, as a Python + Qt
app for Bazzite, built the way the BC250 Bazzite Suite builds its apps (bc250_core bundled, the same install.sh
and launcher). A front page of tiles opens each feature; Escape or Back returns to it. The quiz keeps the Android
rules (42 seconds, plus 5 for a right answer, minus 5 for a wrong one or a skip, longer rounds after a perfect one)
without the Roberto and Moonshie characters; its questions ship as plain JSON. The 56 true/false questions whose
answer carried its explanation after a colon ("False: ...") could never be answered right in the Android app; the
explanation is now a field of its own and is shown with a wrong answer. The APPS category looked its questions up
under "Apps" in the Android app, which the data does not have; here it finds the 100 "App" questions. Scores and
Perfect trophies go to ~/.local/share/bazzite-datstation/scores.json; the quick quiz saves nothing. The settings
menu adds the app to Steam as a non-Steam game with artwork, and removes it again.
